:: test.I.mind
{=

(metadata:
"title", "Test H: Dice and Table Rolls",
)

(display: "block.testNavigation")

<br>
---
<br>

''Testing mind readout''
<br>
$cssDesc[Mind is a number, which corresponds to a level name. `''(passage: "code.mind")'s out''` is used to output the raw string for the current mind's level's name ("dying", "very low", "low", "slightly low", "medium", "slightly high", "very high", or "insane"). It references the table in `''(passage: "code.mind")'s mindLevels''`.
<br>
It is best practice to put the output macro into a temp var so that it can easily be called inside a passage.
]
<br>

<!--refresh short hand-->
(set: _refresh to [(t8n: "dissolve")(rerun: ?TestI1)(rerun: ?sidebarMind)])
<ul>
<li>(link-rerun: "Set player's mind")[{
    (dialog: [(input: bind $player's mind)], "OK")
    (set: $player's mind to (num: $player's mind))
    _refresh
}]</li>
<li>(link-rerun: "Decrease mind")[{
    (set: $player's mind to it -1)
    _refresh
}]</li>
<li>(link-rerun: "Increase mind")[{
    (set: $player's mind to it +1)
    _refresh
}]</li>
<li>(link-rerun: "Reset mind")[{
    (set: $player's mind to 10)
    _refresh
}]</li>
</ul>
<br>
<!--short hand-->
(set: _outputMind to (passage: "code.mind")'s output)
Mind: [(print: $player's mind) ((_outputMind:))]<TestI1|
